===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# That [[scintillate]]s with brief flashes of light; [[sparkling]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1994|author=w:Edward St Aubyn|title=Bad News|page=147|publisher=Picador|year_published=2006
|passage=On the '''scintillating''' water yellow and blue boats bobbed up and down.}}
#* '''2012''' October 13, quoting {{w|Nguyen Chi Thien}}, “Nguyen Chi Thien: Nguyen Chi Thien, a Vietnamese poet, died on October 2nd, aged 73”, in ''{{w|The Economist}}''<sup>[https://web.archive.org/web/20121013085955/http://www.economist.com/node/21564511]</sup>, archived from [http://www.economist.com/node/21564511 the original] on 13 October 2012:
#*: They sank me into the ocean / Wishing me to remain in the depths. / I became a deep sea diver / And came up covered with '''scintillating''' pearls.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} [[brilliantly|Brilliantly]] or [[impressively]] clever, exciting, amusing or [[witty]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1864|author=w:Edgar Allan Poe|title=[[s:The Literati of New York/No. II/Anna Cora Mowatt|The Literati of New York - No. II - Anna Cora Mowatt]]
|passage=Her sketches and tales may be said to be cleverly written. They are lively, easy, conventional, '''scintillating''' with a species of sarcastic wit, which might be termed good were it in any respect original.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=8|passage=The humor of my proposition appealed more strongly to Miss Trevor than I had looked for, and from that time forward she became her old self again;{{nb...}}. Our table in the dining-room became again the abode of '''scintillating''' wit and caustic repartee, Farrar bracing up to his old standard, and the demand for seats in the vicinity rose to an animated competition.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Irvine Paris|title=John Lennon in His Own Wrong: Farcical Poetry or Poetical Farce?|newspaper=w:The Liverpool Herald|date=24 March 1964|passage=For the last thirteen months, [[w:The Beatles|Beatles]] cofounder {{w|John Lennon}} has been Liverpool's darling. He can do no wrong. His group's music is '''scintillating'''. His public demeanor has been exemplary. He is a credit to our city, to rock 'n' roll musicians, and to the undead.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Ian Hughes|title=Southampton 1–2 Man Utd|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/fa_cup/9379065.stm|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160421055009/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/fa_cup/9379065.stm|archivedate=21 April 2016|work=w:BBC Sport|date=29 January 2011|passage=The hosts maintained their discipline and shape, even threatening to grab a second goal on the break&nbsp;– left-back Dan Harding made a '''scintillating''' run, skipping past a few challenges before prodding a right-footed shot that did not match his build-up.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Michelle Goldberg|title=The Book That Explains Our Cultural Stagnation|work=The New York Times|date=2022-08-29|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/29/opinion/status-culture-book.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Lots of people are looking for something '''scintillating''' and new and not finding it.}}

